{"id":"h077","run":2,"role":"test_right","category":"science-physics","question":"What will be the maximum kinetic energy of the photoelectrons ejected from magnesium (for which the work function \\varphi = 3.7eV) when irradiated by ultraviolet light of frequency 1.5 × 10^15 sec^-1 ?\nIs the correct answer \"2.5eV\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"TIGER-Lab/MMLU-Pro, test split","claims":[{"text":"The maximum kinetic energy is given by Einstein's photoelectric equation K_max = hf - phi.","confidence":0.97,"lean":0.5,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The photon energy hf is about 6.20 eV for f = 1.5e15 Hz.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.6,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Subtracting the 3.7 eV work function gives K_max of 2.50 eV.","confidence":0.96,"lean":0.9,"theta":1.508,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The photon energy exceeds the work function, so emission occurs and the result is physically sensible.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.5,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The frequency unit s^-1 without 'Hz' might be misread, for example as a wavelength, giving a very different answer.","confidence":0.1,"lean":-0.3,"theta":0.1571,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Using a rounded value of h could shift the result slightly but not change it from 2.5 eV.","confidence":0.85,"lean":0.4,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The frequency should be taken at face value as 1.5e15 Hz, which is ultraviolet and consistent with the problem.","confidence":0.9,"lean":0.6,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The proposed answer of 2.5 eV is correct.","confidence":0.96,"lean":1,"theta":1.508,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.5,"